# EtPoll Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtPoll` is a compound component for building interactive polls and surveys. It provides:

- **Compound component pattern**: Flexible composition with subcomponents
- **Poll question display**: customizable question text
- **Answer options**: separate components for voting vs. results states
- **Vote visualization**: progress bars showing vote distribution
- **Voter avatars**: displays up to 3 voter avatars
- **Undo functionality**: allows users to retract their vote
- **Results display**: shows percentages and vote counts

**Does NOT handle:**

- Vote submission logic (parent handles API calls)
- Multiple selection (single answer only)
- Real-time vote updates (parent manages data)

## Compound Component API

### Basic Usage

```tsx
<EtPoll answers={answers} voteCount={0}>
  <EtPoll.Frame>
    <EtPoll.Question>What's your investing style?</EtPoll.Question>
    <EtPoll.OptionsList>
      {answers.map((answer) => (
        <EtPoll.VotableOption key={answer.id} answerId={answer.id} />
      ))}
    </EtPoll.OptionsList>
    <EtPoll.FooterContent>
      <EtPoll.VoteCount />
    </EtPoll.FooterContent>
  </EtPoll.Frame>
</EtPoll>
```

### With Results & Voter Avatars

```tsx
<EtPoll answers={answers} voteCount={210} selectedId={selectedAnswer} avatarUrls={avatarUrls} additionalVotersCount={207} onUndo={() => handleUndo()}>
  <EtPoll.Frame>
    <EtPoll.Question>What's your investing style?</EtPoll.Question>
    <EtPoll.OptionsList>
      {answers.map((answer) => (
        <EtPoll.ResultOption key={answer.id} answerId={answer.id} />
      ))}
    </EtPoll.OptionsList>
    <EtPoll.FooterContent>
      <EtPoll.VoterAvatars />
      <EtPoll.UndoButton />
    </EtPoll.FooterContent>
  </EtPoll.Frame>
</EtPoll>
```

> **Note:** `EtPoll.FooterDivider` is still exported for compositions that
> need a separator above the footer, but the canonical Figma poll layout
> (PE-904 / Feed 2026) does not include one. Omit it unless your design
> explicitly calls for the divider.

## Subcomponents

### `EtPoll` (Provider)

The root component that provides context to all subcomponents.

**Props:**

- `answers` (required) - Array of poll answer options
- `voteCount` - Total vote count
- `selectedId` - Currently selected answer ID (controlled)
- `onVote` - Callback when answer is selected
- `onUndo` - Callback when undo is pressed
- `avatarUrls` - Array of avatar URLs (max 3)
- `additionalVotersCount` - Count of additional voters not shown
- `question` - Question text (if not using EtPoll.Question child)
- `children` - Compound components

### `EtPoll.Frame`

Container with card styling: flat translucent overlay (`cardDefault`),
rounded corners (`X4`), and `X5` padding/gap. Per Feed 2026 Figma there
is no shadow or elevation.

**Props:**

- `children` (required) - Poll content
- `style` - Optional style override
- `testID` - Test identifier

### `EtPoll.Question`

Displays the poll question.

**Props:**

- `children` (required) - Question text
- `maxLines` (default: 4) - Max visible lines before "Show more" truncation

**Styling:**

- Text variant: `label-primary-semibold` (Figma "Label/Primary/Semi-bold", 16/600/20)
- Wrapped in `EtReadMoreText` so long questions are collapsible

### `EtPoll.OptionsList`

Container for poll options with proper spacing.

**Props:**

- `children` - Poll option components

### `EtPoll.VotableOption`

Answer option button for **before voting** state.

**Props:**

- `answerId` (required) - ID of the answer to display
- `testID` - Test identifier

**Behavior:**

- Translucent pill button — bg = `${carbon900}14` (theme-aware ~8% black overlay,
  preserved from the pre-PE-904 production value after design review)
- Calls `actions.vote(answerId)` from context when pressed
- Geometry: `paddingVertical: X2`, `paddingHorizontal: X5`, `borderRadius: X9`
- Text variant: `body-secondary-medium` (14 / weight 500), color `carbon900`

### `EtPoll.ResultOption`

Answer option for **after voting** state (shows results).

**Props:**

- `answerId` (required) - ID of the answer to display
- `testID` - Test identifier

**Behavior:**

- Animated progress fill — absolutely-positioned `Animated.View` sized to 100%
  width and `scaleX`-animated 0 → `percentage / 100` from the leading edge
  (`transformOrigin: 'left center'`, `400ms` cubic-out). Selected fill =
  `primary600`; unselected fill = `${carbon900}14` (translucent overlay;
  pre-PE-904 production value preserved)
- Percentage on the right, rounded to integer (e.g. `58%`)
- Selected percentage uses `verdictPositive600`; unselected uses `carbon900`
- Selected label uses `carbon050` (white in light, dark in dark — readable on the
  green pill in both themes); unselected label uses `carbon900`
- No checkmark/icon — Figma uses fill color alone to indicate selection
- Geometry: `paddingVertical: X2`, `paddingHorizontal: X5`, `borderRadius: X9`
- Text variant: `body-secondary-medium` (14 / weight 500)
- Percentage variant: `num-s-medium`

### `EtPoll.VoteCount`

Displays total vote count.

**Behavior:**

- Shows "X Votes" or "1 Vote" (plural/singular)
- Text variant: `label-tertiary-regular`
- Color: `textSecondary` from context

### `EtPoll.VoterAvatars`

Displays up to 3 voter avatars with additional count.

**Behavior:**

- Shows max 3 overlapping avatars
- Shows "+X other voters" text if additionalVotersCount > 0
- Automatically hides if no avatars and no additional count
- Text variant: `label-tertiary-regular`

### `EtPoll.UndoButton`

Button to undo vote.

**Behavior:**

- Calls `actions.undo()` from context when pressed
- Text variant: `label-tertiary-semibold`
- Color: `indicatorPositive` (green)

### `EtPoll.FooterDivider`

Horizontal separator above footer.

**Behavior:**

- Border-top: 1px using theme's divider color

> Not part of the canonical Feed 2026 poll layout (PE-904). Kept in the
> compound API for compositions that explicitly need a divider above the
> footer.

### `EtPoll.FooterContent`

Container for footer items with flex layout.

**Props:**

- `children` - Footer content (VoteCount, VoterAvatars, UndoButton, etc.)

**Behavior:**

- Horizontal layout with space-between

## Common Patterns

### Before Voting

```tsx
<EtPoll answers={answers} voteCount={totalVotes} onVote={handleVote}>
  <EtPoll.Frame>
    <EtPoll.Question>{question}</EtPoll.Question>
    <EtPoll.OptionsList>
      {answers.map((a) => (
        <EtPoll.VotableOption key={a.id} answerId={a.id} />
      ))}
    </EtPoll.OptionsList>
    <EtPoll.FooterContent>
      <EtPoll.VoteCount />
    </EtPoll.FooterContent>
  </EtPoll.Frame>
</EtPoll>
```

### After Voting (with Undo)

```tsx
<EtPoll
  answers={answers}
  voteCount={totalVotes}
  selectedId={userSelection}
  avatarUrls={voterAvatars}
  additionalVotersCount={otherVotersCount}
  onUndo={handleUndo}
>
  <EtPoll.Frame>
    <EtPoll.Question>{question}</EtPoll.Question>
    <EtPoll.OptionsList>
      {answers.map((a) => (
        <EtPoll.ResultOption key={a.id} answerId={a.id} />
      ))}
    </EtPoll.OptionsList>
    <EtPoll.FooterContent>
      <EtPoll.VoterAvatars />
      <EtPoll.UndoButton />
    </EtPoll.FooterContent>
  </EtPoll.Frame>
</EtPoll>
```

`EtPoll.FooterContent` lays out its children with `space-between`, so the
`<EtPoll.UndoButton />` after `<EtPoll.VoterAvatars />` lands on the right.

### Controlled State

```tsx
function MyPollComponent() {
  const [selectedId, setSelectedId] = useState<string | undefined>();

  return (
    <EtPoll
      answers={answers}
      voteCount={totalVotes}
      selectedId={selectedId}
      onVote={(answerId) => {
        setSelectedId(answerId);
        submitVote(answerId);
      }}
      onUndo={() => {
        setSelectedId(undefined);
        retractVote();
      }}
    >
      <EtPoll.Frame>
        <EtPoll.Question>{question}</EtPoll.Question>
        <EtPoll.OptionsList>
          {selectedId
            ? answers.map((a) => <EtPoll.ResultOption key={a.id} answerId={a.id} />)
            : answers.map((a) => <EtPoll.VotableOption key={a.id} answerId={a.id} />)}
        </EtPoll.OptionsList>
        <EtPoll.FooterContent>
          {selectedId ? (
            <>
              <EtPoll.VoterAvatars />
              <EtPoll.UndoButton />
            </>
          ) : (
            <EtPoll.VoteCount />
          )}
        </EtPoll.FooterContent>
      </EtPoll.Frame>
    </EtPoll>
  );
}
```

